@startuml
!include https://static.visual-paradigm.com/web/resources/plantuml-stdlib/themes/vp.puml

title Upload - Upload Image

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam activityFontName Arial
skinparam activityFontSize 14
skinparam activityBorderThickness 1.5
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam ArrowColor #222222
skinparam SwimlaneBorderColor #222222
skinparam SwimlaneBorderThickness 2
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #7DD3FC
  BorderColor #2563EB
  DiamondBackgroundColor #7DD3FC
  DiamondBorderColor #2563EB
  StartColor #111827
  EndColor #FFFFFF
}

|Customer|
start
note right
Precondition:
The customer is signed in.

Postcondition:
The image is on Cloudinary and the app holds its URL to
use as the chat image.
end note
repeat
:Choose an image from the device;
|System|
if (The system fails while processing the request?) then (Yes)
  :Return the system error;
  |Customer|
  :View the system error;
  stop
else (No)
endif
|System|
:Check the caller may upload for this purpose and Cloudinary is configured;
if (The caller is not allowed or Cloudinary is not configured?) then (Yes)
  :Return the upload error;
  |Customer|
  :View the message;
  stop
else (No)
endif
|System|
:Generate a random image id, sign the parameters with the secret and return a signature valid for one hour;
:The app posts the file with the signature to Cloudinary;
backward :Show the upload failure;
repeat while (Cloudinary rejects the file\n(wrong format or expired\nsignature)?) is (Yes) not (No)
:Receive the image URL from Cloudinary;
|Customer|
:View the chosen image;
stop

@enduml
